{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>So he blessed them on that day</b> — The reason for \"on that day\" is that since Joseph was pressing him to put Manasseh first, he declared that he did not wish to remove his right hand from the head of Ephraim onto the head of Manasseh, and not only that, but he went back and said explicitly at that very moment, in Joseph's presence, when he blessed them: \"like Ephraim and like Manasseh.\" <b>So he placed Ephraim before Manasseh</b> in all his blessings." "And the meaning of <b>\"by you shall Israel bless\"</b> — he is speaking to Joseph: for through your seed the nation of Israel shall bless, and one shall say to the one being blessed: \"May Elohim make you like Ephraim and like Manasseh.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "The words כְּאֶפְרַיִם וְכִמְנַשֶּׁה, which Ramban presents as a direct quotation from Jacob's blessing at that moment, refer back to the phrase in Genesis 48:20."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:39.513054324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}